A += [
("Domain 2 skill-area structure (2.1-2.7 organized by technology family)","v1:Domain 2","change","Seven skill areas are technology families (GIS, data management, field technology, analytics, collaboration tools, AI monitoring, immersive tech). About 9 of 35 competencies are almost pure tool fluency (2.3.4, 2.3.5, 2.5.1, 2.5.3, 2.7.1, 2.7.2, 2.7.4 retire; 2.1.3, 2.3.2 largely). Reorganize data craft by durable function along the information chain: Acquire (monitoring/measurement design, field data capture, sensor data engineering), Steward (data management, QC, provenance, publication, sensitive data), Analyze & Model (statistics, spatial, RS, ML/foundation models, process models, forecast systems), Integrate & Communicate (decision support, visual evidence, uncertainty, LLM text analysis), Assure & Govern (AI validation, HITL design, evaluation sets, model risk, procurement, enterprise governance). Tools move to a separate layer (tools_layer_proposal.csv).","J","DC-044|DC-042","DC"),
("Domain 2 proficiency statements","v1:Domain 2 proficiency (Knowledge/Application x 4 levels)","change","Advanced/Expert statements are generic and unobservable across nearly all 35 competencies ('Shapes GIS strategy and standards', 'Provides leadership on ...', 'Expert in ...'). They cannot support hiring or assessment (IO's standard). Replace with scope-of-accountability anchors (own work -> own products -> systems others rely on -> organizational portfolio) and named work products; see datacraft_proficiency_anchors.csv.","E","DC-042","DC"),
("Exposure codes for SA 2.6 in database vs working record","v1:Dimension Tags T13 (2.6.1 T1-T2, 2.6.3 T2, 2.6.5 T2)","needs-evidence","The SA 2.6 working record confirms Auto Type Ac for 2.6.1 T1 and T2 (and A,Ac,A sequences for 2.6.3 and 2.6.5) with Lo tacit/C career for 2.6.1 T1, but the database and normalized baseline record A/Hi/X for 2.6.1 T1 and A for the others (provenance 'Reconstructed (D2)'). DE/LM should reconcile before v2 carries any exposure value forward.","E","DC-046|DC-048","DC"),
("v1 Datacraft definition ('making patterns visible and projecting futures')","v1:craft_assignment_criteria.md","change","Pattern-making and projection are exactly what AI now produces cheaply. The irreducible human data-craft contribution is warrant: producing evidence whose provenance, method, uncertainty and fitness for a decision the practitioner can show and answer for, including when machines did the computation. Redefine accordingly (see report section 3).","J","DC-043|DC-001","DC"),
("Rule 3 (asymmetric error caution: DC over-assignment)","v1:craft_assignment_criteria.md","carry","v1 has 79 DC-primary and 91 DC-secondary tags (170 of 222). Rule 3 was right: Domain 1 science knowledge competencies (e.g., 1.1.1 Ecosystem dynamics, 1.1.3 Succession) are DC primary although their irreducible content is disciplinary knowledge used by all three crafts. Keep Rule 3 and add the knowledge-vs-craft distinction below.","E","DC-042|DC-043","DC"),
("DC-primary tags on Domain 1 science-knowledge competencies (26 of 40)","v1:Dimension Tags (Domain 1)","change","Disciplinary knowledge (ecology, hydrology, climate science, genetics) is the substrate for field, data and state craft alike. Tagging it DC primary inflates data craft and hides its dependence on field and institutional practice. Propose that v2 distinguish knowledge areas from craft practices (craft tags apply to practices; knowledge areas list which crafts draw on them). Decision for CA/IA.","J","DC-042|DC-043","DC"),
("Secondary-FC liberal rule for DC-primary competencies","v1:craft_assignment_criteria.md (note on secondary Fieldcraft)","carry","Carry and strengthen: for any DC competency that validates or applies models/AI describing ecological condition (DC-CAND-09, -10, -13), FC secondary should be required, because out-of-distribution failures are recognized in the field first.","J","DC-043|DC-028","DC"),
("3.4.3 Cryptocurrency, digital payments, and decentralized finance","v1:3.4.3","retire","Tool- and trend-bound; zero blockchain, cryptocurrency or distributed-ledger use cases among 438 USDA/DOI/EPA entries in the 2025 inventory; durable content (financial controls, donor transparency) is covered by 3.4.x and 6.6.x. Move blockchain/crypto to the tools layer as 'watch'.","E","DC-001|DC-042","DC"),
("Tool- and trend-laden task text in 3.4.1, 3.4.4, 3.4.5, 3.6.1, 3.6.2, 3.6.4, 3.6.5, 3.7.1-3.7.5","v1:Domain 3 tasks","change","Nearly every task specifies 'AI-powered', 'IoT', 'blockchain', 'RPA bots' or 'real-time dashboards'. This dates the competencies and makes them unassessable when tools change. Rewrite tasks by function (e.g., 'verify supply-chain material flows' not 'using blockchain and IoT'); move named technologies to the tools layer.","J","DC-042","DC"),
("6.7.2 T1 'Use environmental justice screening tools (EJSCREEN, CalEnviroScreen)'","v1:6.7.2","change","Named public tools are volatile; my understanding is that EPA removed EJScreen from its website in early 2025 (expert recollection, not re-verified this session - LM/DB to confirm). Rewrite as 'apply cumulative-burden screening methods and evaluate the indicators and data behind them'; tools to tools layer.","J","DC-042","DC"),
("6.3.2 T2 'Use tools like InVEST or ARIES'","v1:6.3.2","change","Tool names in task text; move to tools layer and state the durable method (ecosystem-service production-function modeling and validation).","J","DC-042","DC"),
("6.4.4 Public comment management (T2 classified S - substitution)","v1:6.4.4","needs-evidence","Deployed and piloted comment tools are documented as supplemental with analyst verification (FWS DocketScope; EPA Region 8 pilot; USDA pilot) and DOI's PCAT was retired between inventories (DC-001). Current evidence supports Ac/V (compressed, supervised), not S. LM owns exposure coding; DC recommends re-coding and linking to DC-CAND-16.","E","DC-001","DC"),
("6.1.1 / 6.1.2 / 6.4.1 tasks coded S (substitution)","v1:6.1.1 T2|6.1.2 T2|6.4.1 T1","needs-evidence","No USDA/DOI/EPA use case in the 2025 inventory reports AI as the principal basis for policy comparison or compliance determinations: EPA's high-impact cases prioritize inspections or pre-review documents, and the USDA permitting tool is explicitly 'recommendations for authorized staff to review'. S calls need direct evidence (LM lane).","E","DC-001","DC"),
("F7 Environmental Data Science family Core list","v1:Dimension Tags F7","change","F7 is Core for every Domain 2 competency, including virtual meetings, project management software and VR education. Re-derive F7 Core from the durable data-craft functions; retired tool competencies should not define a profession family.","E","DC-042","DC"),
("7.2 skill area coherence (Delphi flag 8)","v1:7.2","change","Answer to v1's Delphi question: keep a Human-AI practice cluster, but as a cross-cutting 'Assure & Govern' function of data craft that also carries SC-secondary competencies; populate the never-drafted 7.2.4-7.2.5 with DC-CAND-16 and DC-CAND-17.","J","DC-045","DC"),
("Universal data and AI literacy (absent)","v1:none","add","v1 has no competency every practitioner is expected to hold for using data and AI. Add DC-CAND-01 and DC-CAND-02 as Tier DC-1 universal competencies (assessed at Foundational for all, higher for some).","E","DC-015|DC-013|DC-017","DC"),
("Data provenance, sensitive-data protection, model risk, AI procurement, evaluation sets (absent)","v1:none","add","See DC-CAND-05, -07, -15, -19, -20. Each is evidenced in federal policy or deployments and missing from v1.","E","DC-002|DC-029|DC-007|DC-008|DC-037","DC"),
("4.5.4 Drone/UAS operation and 2.3.2 Drone operation (duplicate)","v1:4.5.4|v1:2.3.2","change","Merge; FC primary for flight operations and safety; DC secondary for processing and accuracy.","J","DC-042","DC"),
("4.1.5 Digital data collection and management vs 2.3.3/2.3.4 (overlap)","v1:4.1.5|v1:2.3.3|v1:2.3.4","change","Three overlapping competencies for the same function; merge into one field data capture competency (DC primary, FC secondary) with FC-owned observation content kept in 4.1.x.","J","DC-042","DC"),
]
with open(OUTA,"w",newline="",encoding="utf-8") as f:
    w=csv.writer(f); w.writerow(H)
